      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(anthropic): seed API-key default models using own entries",
        "body": "### What Problem This Solves\n\nAnthropic API-key model defaulting used `in` when deciding whether an allowlisted model ref already existed. If `Object.prototype` contains one of those model refs, default seeding skips creating an own model entry, leaving the effective config dependent on process-global prototype state.\n\n### Why This Change Was Made\n\nUse an own-property check before skipping allowlist seeding. Existing own model entries are still preserved, while inherited prototype refs no longer block the canonical default entry from being written.\n\n### User Impact\n\nAPI-key Anthropic profiles get the expected own default model entries even when process-global prototype state contains an allowlisted model ref. Existing own model config remains unchanged.\n\n### Evidence\n\nExact head: `7a86b1502271f68dbac5ede7df6e04e8a5cf9bbe`\n\nBehavior covered by `extensions/anthropic/config-defaults.own-entries.test.ts`:\n\n- temporarily defines a writable `Object.prototype[\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5\"]` entry;\n- verifies the defaults pass writes an own `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5` model entry with `cacheRetention: \"short\"`;\n- verifies existing own model config is preserved;\n- restores the prior `Object.prototype` descriptor in `finally`.\n\nThis replaces the previous custom-prototype test, which was not a valid base/head regression because `{ ...defaults.models }` discards that custom prototype before the changed check runs.\n\nValidation run:\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/anthropic/config-defaults.own-entries.test.ts` (1 test passed)\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1 extensions/anthropic/config-defaults.own-entries.test.ts`\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxlint --threads=1 extensions/anthropic/config-defaults.own-entries.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.extensions.test.json --incremental false --pretty false`\n- `env -u OPENAI_API_KEY -u OPENAI_ORG_ID -u OPENAI_PROJECT_ID .agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local` (exit 0, no findings)\n",
        "branch": "alix/anthropic-api-key-own-default-models",
        "head_sha": "7a86b1502271f68dbac5ede7df6e04e8a5cf9bbe",
